WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.340
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.
我们也是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为你制作了这档终极《办公室》重温播客。

6
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.560
We're The Office Ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:26.280
Hey!
嘿！

9
00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.900
Is everybody ready for Season 8?
大家都准备好迎接第八季了吗？

10
00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:30.720
Season 8.
第八季。

11
00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:32.180
Here it is.
来了。

12
00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:32.800
Ocho.
Ocho（西班牙语：八）。

13
00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:34.500
We're doing it.
我们要开始了。

14
00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:35.300
De la pan.
De la pan（印尼语：八）。

15
00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:37.280
Sorry, that's 8 in Indonesian.
抱歉，那是印尼语里的八。

16
00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:40.540
Okay, no, I'm done.
好吧，不闹了，我结束了。

17
00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:41.360
All right.
好的。

18
00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:43.940
Today is The LiSt.
今天我们要讲的是《名单》。

19
00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:47.180
It is Season 8, Episode 1, written by B.J.
这是第八季第一集，由B.J.诺瓦克编剧，

20
00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:48.980
Novak, directed by B.J.
由B.J.诺瓦克执导。

21
00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:49.580
Novak.
诺瓦克。

22
00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:54.980
Angela, Season 8 was a very emotional rollercoaster of a year for me on The Office.
安吉拉，第八季对我来说是《办公室》里情绪起伏非常大的一年。

23
00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:57.860
First of all, I was very pregnant.
首先，我当时怀着孕。

24
00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:02.540
Then I came back to work after only five weeks.
然后我只休了五周产假就回来工作了。

25
00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:04.920
And we didn't have Steve.
而且史蒂夫也不在了。

26
00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:06.520
It was a year.
真是漫长的一年。

27
00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:07.740
Yeah.
确实。

28
00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:11.380
It's really hard to go back to work when you have a baby.
生完孩子后回去工作真的很难。

29
00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:12.420
It just is.
事实就是这样。

30
00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:16.580
And there were some circumstances that made it harder, but we'll share about that when we get there.
当时还有一些特殊情况让情况变得更糟，但等聊到那儿时我们会细说的。

31
00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:17.480
We'll get to that.
我们会聊到的。

32
00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:18.380
Down the road.
以后再说。

33
00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:20.880
Let's start this episode with a summary.
让我们先从这一集的剧情梗概开始吧。

34
00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:25.460
Andy Bernard is our new Dunder Mifflin Branch Manager.
安迪·伯纳德成了我们邓德·米福林分公司的新经理。

35
00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:30.620
And Robert California is the new CEO of Saber.
罗伯特·加州则是赛博公司的新任首席执行官。

36
00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:33.020
He talked Joe out of her own job.
他竟然说服了乔放弃了自己的职位。

37
00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:34.720
That made me laugh out loud.
这让我忍不住大笑出声。

38
00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:41.620
In this episode, Aaron is going to discover that Robert California has made a list of employees in his notebook.
在这一集中，艾琳发现罗伯特·加州在他的笔记本里列了一份员工名单。

39
00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:44.360
And he has divided this list into two groups.
他把这份名单分成了两组。

40
00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:46.020
But what do the groups mean?
但这两组到底代表什么意思呢？

41
00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:49.120
The office makes it their mission to figure it out.
办公室里的同事们决定要把这件事查个水落石出。

42
00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:53.960
Meanwhile, Angela got married to the state senator over the summer.
与此同时，安吉拉在夏天嫁给了州参议员。

43
00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:56.840
And both Angela and Pam are pregnant.
而且安吉拉和帕姆都怀孕了。

44
00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:59.200
And Pam cannot stop crying.
帕姆一直哭个不停。

45
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:00.640
Pam.
帕姆。

46
00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:02.440
Pam was breaking my heart.
帕姆当时真是让我心碎。

47
00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:05.760
Are you ready for Fast Fact No.
准备好听第一个快速事实了吗？

48
00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:06.180
1?
1？

49
00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:06.900
I am.
准备好了。

50
00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:08.420
Our Fast Fact No.
我们的快速事实编号

51
00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:10.760
1 is called New Manager.
1被称为“新经理”。

52
00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:12.480
That's right.
没错。

53
00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:14.020
Andy Bernard.
安迪·伯纳德。

54
00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:15.960
How did this all come about?
这一切是怎么发生的呢？

55
00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:21.300
Well, as I said before, there was no decision about who was going to take over as manager when we ended Season 7.
嗯，正如我之前所说，第七季结束时，关于谁来接任经理并没有定论。

56
00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:22.980
We all left for our summer break.
我们都去放暑假了。

57
00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:23.540
We didn't know.
我们当时不知道。

58
00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:24.540
We had no idea.
我们完全没头绪。

59
00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:27.020
It was a very interesting summer for our writers.
对我们的编剧来说，那是一个非常有趣的夏天。

60
00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:32.540
And thanks to many messages that I exchanged with BJ Novak and Paul Lieberstein,
多亏了我与BJ·诺瓦克和保罗·利伯斯坦交换的许多信息，

61
00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:36.520
and from reading Andy Green's book and doing some Googling,
以及阅读安迪·格林的书和进行了一些谷歌搜索，

62
00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:39.560
I have the dish on how it all came about.
我掌握了这一切是如何发生的内幕。

63
00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:41.480
Ooh, give it to us.
噢，快告诉我们。

64
00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:42.000
All right.
好的。

65
00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:46.260
The first debate was outside hire versus inside hire.
最初的争论是关于从外部聘请还是内部提拔。

66
00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:48.060
This debate, I remember well.
这场争论，我记忆犹新。

67
00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:50.000
It was swirling around for a while.
它持续发酵了一段时间。

68
00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:52.980
Well, the general consensus was inside hire.
嗯，普遍的共识是内部提拔。

69
00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:53.760
Yeah.
是的。

70
00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:58.760
However, the network liked the idea of an outside hire.
然而，电视网喜欢从外部聘请的想法。

71
00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:05.360
So, our writers did entertain this idea, and the biggest name being tossed around was James Gandolfini.
所以，我们的编剧确实考虑过这个想法，当时被提及的最大牌人选是詹姆斯·甘多菲尼。

72
00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:07.560
I remember this, Jenna.
我记得这件事，珍娜。

73
00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:08.380
You do?
你记得？

74
00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:09.380
Yeah, I do.
是的，我记得。

75
00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:10.260
I remember, too.
我也记得。

76
00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:17.140
Paul Lieberstein, BJ Novak, and Danny Chun all met with James Gandolfini about coming in as our new manager.
保罗·利伯斯坦、BJ·诺瓦克和丹尼·春都与詹姆斯·甘多菲尼见过面，商谈他担任我们新经理的事宜。

77
00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:21.280
And in Andy Green's book, which, by the way, is called The Office,
在安迪·格林的书里——顺便说一下，书名叫《办公室：

78
00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:24.900
The Untold Story of the Greatest Sitcom of the 2000s,
2000年代最伟大情景喜剧的未讲述故事》——

79
00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:29.240
Danny Chun shared that James had seen a few episodes of the show,
丹尼·春分享说，詹姆斯看过几集这部剧，

80
00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:31.520
and he was very complimentary and very interested.
他给予了高度评价，也非常感兴趣。

81
00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:35.540
BJ Novak told me that when they met with him,
BJ·诺瓦克告诉我，当他们与他会面时，

82
00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:39.400
he was super nervous because James Gandolfini was his favorite actor.
他超级紧张，因为詹姆斯·甘多菲尼是他最喜欢的演员。

83
00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:44.020
And he said that James Gandolfini was pretty shy during the meeting,
他说詹姆斯·甘多菲尼在会议期间相当害羞，

84
00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:48.600
but also BJ and Paul and Danny were very shy as well.
但BJ、保罗和丹尼也同样非常害羞。

85
00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:50.120
And so it was a very quiet meeting.
所以那是一场非常安静的会议。

86
00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:51.580
Nobody said very much.
没人说太多话。

87
00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:52.700
They just kind of sat there.
他们只是坐在那里。

88
00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:54.820
We were all obsessed with The Sopranos.
我们当时都迷恋《黑道家族》。

89
00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:59.340
Let me tell you, if Tony Soprano had walked onto that soundstage,
我跟你说，如果托尼·索普拉诺走进那个摄影棚，

90
00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:00.180
I would have been like,
我会表现得像……

91
00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:03.980
All right, so here is the character that they had in mind.
好了，这就是他们构想中的角色。

92
00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:05.740
This is how Danny described it.
丹尼是这样描述的。

93
00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:06.440
Quote,
引用如下：

94
00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:12.160
Salt of the earth, intense, passionate guy who could be your father figure and your biggest supporter
“脚踏实地、热烈、充满激情的家伙，他既可以是你的父亲形象，也可以是你最大的支持者，

95
00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:15.440
and the most sort of wonderful person to have on your side,
是你站在你这边最棒的人，

96
00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:19.300
but also turn around and be the scariest person you've ever seen in your life
但转过头来，他也可以是你一生中见过的最可怕的人，

97
00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:20.840
and just bite your head off about something.
因为某件事直接把你骂得狗血淋头。”

98
00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:26.240
So this was the character they were imagining that James Gandolfini would play in a comedic way.
所以这就是他们想象中詹姆斯·甘多菲尼会以喜剧方式演绎的角色。

99
00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:27.960
This was a comic turn.
这是一次喜剧性的尝试。

100
00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:30.280
But ultimately, it didn't work out.
但最终，这件事没成。

101
00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:35.800
Now, there was a little dish served up recently on the podcast Talking Sopranos.
最近在播客《Talking Sopranos》里有个小插曲。

102
00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:40.820
That is the podcast where the stars of The Sopranos, it's Michael Imperioli and Steve Schirippa.
那是《黑道家族》主演迈克尔·因佩里奥利和史蒂夫·斯基里帕主持的播客。

103
00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:42.480
They tell stories about Sopranos.
他们在节目里讲述《黑道家族》的幕后故事。

104
00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:42.760
Yeah.
没错。

105
00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:47.220
Everyone, you should listen if you want to hear some breakdown about The Sopranos.
大家如果想听关于《黑道家族》的深度解析，一定要去听听。

106
00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:53.060
But they talked about this moment where James Gandolfini was possibly going to come on The Office.
但他们聊到了詹姆斯·甘多菲尼差点要来客串《办公室》的那件事。

107
00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:55.780
And Steve Schirippa said,
史蒂夫·斯基里帕说：

108
00:04:55.960 --> 00:05:03.460
We made him an offer, but that HBO countered our offer and paid him $3 million not to take the role.
“我们向他发出了邀请，但HBO反过来给了他300万美元，让他别接这个角色。”

109
00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:04.580
Jeez.
天哪。

110
00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:05.480
Yeah.
是啊。

111
00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:09.140
Now, I did some fact checking on that.
我为此做了一些事实核查。

112
00:05:09.420 --> 00:05:15.320
My sources tell me that we never made a financial offer to James Gandolfini to do the show.
我的消息来源告诉我，我们从未向詹姆斯·甘多菲尼提供过具体的片酬报价。

113
00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:16.240
Are these your secret sources?
这是你那些秘密消息来源吗？

114
00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:17.620
These are my secret sources.
没错，就是我的秘密消息来源。

115
00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:18.440
Secret.
秘密的。

116
00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:24.020
But that James Gandolfini ultimately decided that he wanted to do a development deal with HBO
但詹姆斯·甘多菲尼最终决定与HBO签订一份开发协议，

117
00:05:24.020 --> 00:05:27.740
and do some other projects rather than get locked into a TV contract.
去做些别的项目，而不是被锁死在一部电视剧的合同里。

118
00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:31.680
So, I guess HBO did make him a deal.
所以，我想HBO确实给了他一份合约。

119
00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:37.720
Maybe that, you know, stopped any potential deal in its tracks with us.
也许这确实阻碍了我们与他达成合作的任何可能性。

120
00:05:37.880 --> 00:05:41.760
But my sources say an offer was not officially made.
但我的消息来源说，我们并没有正式发出过报价。

121
00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:42.520
Okay.
好吧。

122
00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:48.660
So, after all of this, the writers decided, for sure, we're going to do an inside hire.
所以，经过这一切，编剧们确定要从内部提拔人选。

123
00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:50.820
That had been their first instinct, you know?
这本来就是他们的第一直觉，你知道吧？

124
00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:51.060
Right.
没错。

125
00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:53.720
Krista D from Allendale, Illinois said,
来自伊利诺伊州阿伦代尔的克里斯塔·D问道：

126
00:05:53.860 --> 00:06:00.400
Did the writers choose Andy to become the Scranton branch manager because he's the most likely to be a yes man to corporate?
“编剧们选择安迪担任斯克兰顿分部经理，是因为他最有可能成为总公司的唯命是从者吗？”

127
00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:04.180
Was there a lot of discussion around who would take over as manager?
“关于谁来接任经理，当时有很多讨论吗？”

128
00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:05.460
Oh, Krista.
噢，克里斯塔。

129
00:06:05.980 --> 00:06:07.500
There was so much discussion.
讨论多得不得了。

130
00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:09.040
There was lots of chatter.
当时有很多议论。

131
00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:12.740
Writer Danny Chun said the discussions got quite heated.
编剧丹尼·春说讨论过程相当激烈。

132
00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:17.220
Paul Lieberstein said here was their criteria for picking a new boss.
保罗·李伯斯坦说，这是他们挑选新老板的标准。

133
00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:18.360
Quote,
引用如下：

134
00:06:18.700 --> 00:06:25.180
One of the important aspects is that the boss puts something into the relationships in the office that is not just professional.
“其中一个重要方面是，老板要能为办公室的人际关系注入一些非职业性的东西。”

135
00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:28.500
They have to see it as a lot more than what it is.
“他们必须把这份工作看得比它本身更重要。”

136
00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:35.340
And they decided that the two people who would take the job of manager most personally were Andy or Dwight.
他们认为，最会把经理这份工作当回事的两个人就是安迪或德怀特。

137
00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:37.280
Okay, that tracks.
好吧，这说得通。

138
00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:41.140
People argued heavily for each side.
大家为支持各自的人选争论得很激烈。

139
00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:46.940
If you want to read everyone's passionate feelings about this, it is all in Andy Green's book.
如果你想了解每个人对此的热切想法，安迪·格林的书中都有记载。

140
00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:51.040
There's a lot of stuff in Andy Green's book that I knew already.
安迪·格林的书里有很多我本来就知道的事情。

141
00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:51.960
Like, we knew.
比如，我们都知道的那些。

142
00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:52.380
Right.
没错。

143
00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:58.300
This was a glimpse into the writer's room that I found very interesting.
这让我得以一窥编剧室的情况，我觉得非常有趣。

144
00:06:58.340 --> 00:06:59.880
So just putting that out there.
所以就顺便提一下。

145
00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:05.700
So maybe the real list was a notepad and on one side was Andy and on the other side was Dwight.
所以也许那份真正的名单只是个记事本，一边写着安迪，另一边写着德怀特。

146
00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:06.400
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

147
00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:07.160
I think you're right.
我想你是对的。

148
00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:07.540
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

149
00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:12.580
I remember Paul called me into his office and he asked me my opinion.
我记得保罗把我叫进他的办公室，问了我的意见。

150
00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:15.820
Did I think it should be Andy or Dwight?
问我觉得应该是安迪还是德怀特？

151
00:07:16.440 --> 00:07:17.580
I said, Dwight.
我说的是德怀特。

152
00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:19.400
I'm sorry, Ed.
抱歉，埃德。

153
00:07:19.560 --> 00:07:21.800
I just really wanted it for Dwight.
我只是真的很想让德怀特得到它。

154
00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:26.540
You know, the character of Dwight has wanted this for so long.
你知道，德怀特这个角色渴望这个机会已经很久了。

155
00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:28.640
I think I wanted that dream fulfillment for him.
我想我是想帮他实现那个梦想。

156
00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:30.380
So I picked Dwight.
所以我选了德怀特。

157
00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:32.700
Here were a couple of their concerns.
以下是他们当时的一些顾虑。

158
00:07:33.420 --> 00:07:38.520
Their concern was that having Dwight as the manager meant that we would lose our main antagoniSt.
他们的顾虑是，让德怀特当经理意味着我们会失去主要的对立角色。

159
00:07:39.260 --> 00:07:39.700
Right.
没错。

160
00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:40.440
Right.
对。

161
00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:41.120
That is fair.
这很合理。

162
00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:46.000
And you would lose that foil between Jim and Dwight because now Dwight would be Jim's boss.
而且你会失去吉姆和德怀特之间的那种制衡，因为现在德怀特成了吉姆的上司。

163
00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:46.440
Yes.
是的。

164
00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:46.780
Yeah.
没错。

165
00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:55.580
But they were also concerned that the character of Andy becoming manager would feel too similar to Michael Scott and it would be harder to distinguish him from Michael.
但他们也担心安迪这个角色如果成为经理，会感觉太像迈克尔·斯科特，很难将他与迈克尔区分开来。

166
00:07:55.920 --> 00:07:58.060
And they were trying to wrap their head around that.
他们当时正试图理清这一点。

167
00:07:58.380 --> 00:08:05.800
Well, right around this time, The Hangover 2 came out and it earned over $500 million at the box office.
正好就在那个时候，《宿醉2》上映了，票房收入超过了5亿美元。

168
00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:08.420
This was so huge.
这太轰动了。

169
00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:15.960
I mean, it catapulted Ed into this whole new stratosphere of like, I don't know, showbiz.
我的意思是，这让埃德一跃进入了演艺圈的一个全新高度。

170
00:08:16.540 --> 00:08:17.320
Well, guess what?
你猜怎么着？

171
00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:20.520
The network had a real strong feeling about it after that.
在那之后，电视网对此有了非常强烈的预感。

172
00:08:20.740 --> 00:08:22.020
I bet they did.
我敢打赌他们肯定有。

173
00:08:22.380 --> 00:08:26.720
And that tipped the scales in favor of Ed taking over the role.
这让天平向埃德接手这个角色倾斜了。

174
00:08:27.460 --> 00:08:28.620
Fast fact number two.
第二个快讯。

175
00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:30.300
Are you ready for this dish?
准备好听听这个八卦了吗？

176
00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:31.060
Yeah.
好的。

177
00:08:31.340 --> 00:08:33.380
This one is called New CEO.
这一条叫做“新任CEO”。

178
00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:37.500
Fan question from Michaela G in Wisconsin.
来自威斯康星州米凯拉·G的粉丝提问。

179
00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:41.880
In this episode, James Spader takes over the role of CEO for Kathy Bates.
在这一集中，詹姆斯·斯派德接替凯西·贝茨担任CEO一职。

180
00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:47.920
Is there a reason why they had James Spader join the cast instead of keeping Kathy Bates as the CEO?
他们让詹姆斯·斯派德加入剧组，而不是让凯西·贝茨继续担任CEO，是有什么原因吗？

181
00:08:48.940 --> 00:08:50.280
Yes, Michaela.
是的，米凯拉。

182
00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:56.340
Kathy Bates landed on a new TV series she was the star of called Harry's Law.
凯西·贝茨接拍了一部新电视剧，她是该剧的主演，剧名叫《律政俏师太》。

183
00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:58.240
She was not available to be our CEO.
她没法继续担任我们的CEO了。

184
00:08:58.520 --> 00:08:59.360
Was she Harry?
她叫哈利吗？

185
00:08:59.780 --> 00:09:01.200
Like, was her last name Harry?
我是说，她姓哈利吗？

186
00:09:01.460 --> 00:09:02.020
I don't know.
我不知道。

187
00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:06.060
Well, if she's the star and it's Harry's Law, I have no idea.
好吧，如果她是主演，剧名又叫《律政俏师太》，我真不知道。

188
00:09:06.680 --> 00:09:08.080
Sorry, I'm just curious.
抱歉，我只是好奇。

189
00:09:11.180 --> 00:09:16.380
Okay, Cassie just said that Harry's Law, Harry is short for Harriet.
好了，卡西刚才说《律政俏师太》里的哈利是哈丽特的缩写。

190
00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:18.000
All right.
好吧。

191
00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:20.180
So we don't have a CEO anymore.
所以我们没有CEO了。

192
00:09:20.180 --> 00:09:21.340
We need a new CEO.
我们需要一位新CEO。

193
00:09:21.860 --> 00:09:23.140
Here's something that happened.
事情是这样的。

194
00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:27.540
Over the summer, people freaked out over the character of Robert California.
那个夏天，人们对罗伯特·加利福尼亚这个角色感到非常疯狂。

195
00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:28.960
As they should.
理应如此。

196
00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:29.620
Yes.
没错。

197
00:09:29.820 --> 00:09:30.880
He is delicious.
他太有魅力了。

198
00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:33.580
The head of the network loved James Spader.
电视网负责人很喜欢詹姆斯·斯派德。

199
00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:35.620
The writers loved James Spader.
编剧们也很喜欢詹姆斯·斯派德。

200
00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:37.300
He was an audience favorite.
他是观众的最爱。

201
00:09:37.820 --> 00:09:40.140
They were like, maybe James Spader could be our new CEO.
他们当时想，也许詹姆斯·斯派德能成为我们的新任首席执行官。

202
00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:42.780
They didn't know if they could convince him to do it.
他们不知道能不能说服他接下这个职位。

203
00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:45.600
It was like a big thing when they pitched him the cameo.
当他们向他提议客串时，这可是件大事。

204
00:09:45.740 --> 00:09:46.500
They're like, don't worry.
他们说，别担心。

205
00:09:46.620 --> 00:09:47.400
It's one episode.
就一集。

206
00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:48.280
It's one thing.
就这一件事。

207
00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:49.640
You'll be in and out.
你很快就能搞定。

208
00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:51.880
Turns out he loved doing our show.
结果他很喜欢我们的节目。

209
00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:52.940
He had a great experience.
他有很棒的体验。

210
00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:58.080
But there was another reason why he accepted the role, which was revealed in Andy Green's book.
但他接受这个角色的另一个原因，在安迪·格林的书中揭晓了。

211
00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:00.380
And, oh, my God, it is amazing.
天哪，这太绝了。

212
00:10:00.880 --> 00:10:02.580
I love James Spader so much.
我太喜欢詹姆斯·斯派德了。

213
00:10:03.340 --> 00:10:09.080
He said he took the role because he liked the show and also because he was basically broke and needed the money.
他说他接下这个角色是因为他喜欢这部剧，也因为他当时基本上破产了，需要钱。

214
00:10:11.720 --> 00:10:13.920
He said this is so him.
他说这太像他的风格了。

215
00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:15.160
I can hear him saying this.
我能想象他说这话的样子。

216
00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:19.860
He said he'd just done a big renovation on his house and he'd spent all of his Boston legal money.
他说他刚给房子做了大翻修，花光了他在《波士顿法律》里赚的所有钱。

217
00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:21.880
He needed the paycheck, guys.
伙计们，他需要那笔薪水。

218
00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:22.280
Yeah.
没错。

219
00:10:22.460 --> 00:10:26.940
He'd also just done a play on Broadway for a whole year, which, as we know, does not pay a lot.
他还刚在百老汇演了一整年的戏，众所周知，那赚不了多少钱。

220
00:10:27.320 --> 00:10:34.140
And he said this when the play was done, quote, I knew I was going to need some money because I was hemorrhaging cash doing the play.
他在戏演完后说了这样一段话，引用如下：“我知道我需要钱，因为演这部戏让我一直在亏钱。”

221
00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:36.340
And then all of a sudden I got a call from the office.
然后突然间，我接到了《办公室》剧组的电话。

222
00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:42.820
Now, we initially called him about just doing an arc on the show, just kind of like popping in from time to time like Kathy Bates had done.
起初，我们只是联系他想让他来客串一段，就像凯西·贝茨那样偶尔露个面。

223
00:10:43.380 --> 00:10:50.020
But at the time, he was also in talks to do the Steven Spielberg movie, Lincoln, which he really wanted to do.
但当时他也在商谈出演史蒂文·斯皮尔伯格的电影《林肯》，他非常想演那部戏。

224
00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:51.600
And it seemed like it was going to be a conflict.
而且看起来这会产生档期冲突。

225
00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:55.040
He said they were doing the movie, Lincoln, on a really reduced budget.
他说他们拍《林肯》这部电影时预算非常吃紧。

226
00:10:55.040 --> 00:10:56.940
It was not going to be a big paycheck.
那不会是一笔丰厚的报酬。

227
00:10:57.440 --> 00:10:59.620
And the movie wasn't going to start for eight months.
而且电影八个月后才开拍。

228
00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:04.620
And he said he really wanted you to know, quote, by this point, I was broke.
他说他真的很想让你知道，引用如下：“到这个时候，我已经破产了。”

229
00:11:04.880 --> 00:11:06.180
Really, I was broke.
真的，我破产了。

230
00:11:07.340 --> 00:11:14.980
So he told his agents to go back to the office and say he would do the part for one year, but it had to be for a full season.
所以他让经纪人回去告诉剧组，他愿意出演这个角色一年，但必须是完整的一季。

231
00:11:15.260 --> 00:11:18.960
And he needed time off to do the movie, Lincoln, if it came together.
而且如果《林肯》开拍的话，他需要请假去拍电影。

232
00:11:19.160 --> 00:11:20.640
He needed to get that coin.
他需要赚那笔钱。

233
00:11:20.900 --> 00:11:25.080
Listen, Jen and I are laughing because I can hear his voice.
听着，我和简在笑是因为我能听到他的声音。

234
00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:26.260
I can, too.
我也能。

235
00:11:26.320 --> 00:11:28.080
He's so earnest when he says something.
他说起话来总是那么诚恳。

236
00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:30.320
It's like the man cannot lie.
就像这个人根本不会撒谎一样。

237
00:11:30.520 --> 00:11:33.160
He just tells you exactly his thoughts.
他只是如实说出自己的想法。

238
00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:38.680
The quotes made me smile because it was the same James Spader that we loved being on set with.
这些引语让我笑了，因为这就是我们所爱的那位在片场共事的詹姆斯·斯派德。

239
00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:41.220
He is just no BS.
他就是这么直率，不玩虚的。

240
00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:42.600
No, straightforward.
没错，开门见山。

241
00:11:42.980 --> 00:11:44.240
I just loved him.
我真是太喜欢他了。

242
00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:44.960
Same.
我也是。

243
00:11:45.400 --> 00:11:46.940
So it worked out.
所以事情就这样成了。

244
00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:48.280
James Spader got the role.
詹姆斯·斯派德拿到了这个角色。

245
00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:58.320
Well, I came across an article in Entertainment Weekly from July 6, 2011, and Paul Lieberstein was asked about James taking over as CEO.
嗯，我偶然发现了一篇2011年7月6日的《娱乐周刊》文章，保罗·利伯斯坦被问及詹姆斯接任首席执行官的事。

246
00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:00.300
And this is what he said.
他是这么说的。

247
00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:10.560
James will reprise his role as Robert California, the uber-salesman that has a power to convince and manipulate like a high-class weirdo Jedi warrior.
詹姆斯将继续饰演罗伯特·加利福尼亚，这位超级推销员有着像高级怪咖绝地武士一样令人信服和操纵人心的力量。

248
00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:16.200
He'll have been hired over the summer as the new manager, but within hours gets himself promoted.
他会在夏天被聘为新经理，但几小时内就让自己升职了。

249
00:12:16.600 --> 00:12:18.480
Within days, he takes over the company.
几天之内，他就接管了公司。

250
00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:24.580
James has an energy that is completely his own, and the office has no tools for dealing with this guy.
詹姆斯有一种完全属于他自己的能量，而《办公室》里的人根本没法应付这家伙。

251
00:12:24.780 --> 00:12:27.060
We are thrilled he's joining our caSt.
我们非常高兴他能加入我们的剧组。

252
00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:28.560
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

253
00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:29.640
And we were.
我们当时也是。

254
00:12:29.780 --> 00:12:30.680
We were so excited.
我们当时太兴奋了。

255
00:12:30.940 --> 00:12:32.260
I have so many stories.
我有很多故事要讲。

256
00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:33.820
We have so many stories.
我们有很多故事要讲。

257
00:12:34.220 --> 00:12:39.820
We share some in our book, The Office BFFs, you guys, about our mornings in hair and makeup with James.
我们在书《办公室闺蜜》里分享了一些，伙计们，关于我们和詹姆斯在化妆间度过的清晨时光。

258
00:12:41.420 --> 00:12:43.100
Are you ready for Fast Fact No.
准备好迎接第三个冷知识了吗？

259
00:12:43.180 --> 00:12:43.420
3?
第三个？

260
00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:44.220
Yes.
准备好了。

261
00:12:44.460 --> 00:12:47.440
It's called Big Preggs, Little Preggs.
这个冷知识叫“大肚婆，小肚婆”。

262
00:12:47.440 --> 00:12:47.880
Yes!
没错！

263
00:12:48.100 --> 00:12:52.380
Because we were so excited to have this storyline together.
因为我们当时太兴奋能一起演这条故事线了。

264
00:12:52.380 --> 00:12:53.720
Do you remember at the table read?
你还记得剧本围读的时候吗？

265
00:12:53.940 --> 00:12:54.460
Yes!
记得！

266
00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:55.720
We were giddy.
我们当时兴奋得不得了。

267
00:12:55.940 --> 00:12:59.380
And Jenna, I found an email I sent to Steve about it.
还有珍娜，我找到了一封我发给史蒂夫关于这件事的邮件。

268
00:12:59.660 --> 00:13:00.020
What?
什么？

269
00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:00.720
Yes!
真的！

270
00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:02.180
In my digital clutter.
在我那些杂乱的电子文档里。

271
00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:03.840
You have to hear this.
你一定要听听这个。

272
00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:05.060
Hey, Steve.
嘿，史蒂夫。

273
00:13:05.320 --> 00:13:06.220
How are you guys?
你们好吗？

274
00:13:06.580 --> 00:13:08.240
Congrats on your Emmy nomination.
恭喜你获得艾美奖提名。

275
00:13:08.540 --> 00:13:10.440
Okay, first of all, you so deserve it.
首先，你是实至名归。

276
00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:14.380
But selfishly, we are so excited because it means we get to see you guys.
但自私地说，我们太兴奋了，因为这意味着我们又能见到你们了。

277
00:13:15.240 --> 00:13:17.540
This week, we went back for season eight.
这周，我们回到了第八季的拍摄。

278
00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:20.940
They have some really fun storylines for Pam and Angela.
他们为帕姆和安吉拉安排了一些非常有趣的剧情。

279
00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:23.100
We get to be real frenemies again.
我们又能变回真正的“友敌”了。

280
00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:24.820
And Jenna and I are so excited.
珍娜和我对此都非常兴奋。

281
00:13:25.020 --> 00:13:26.280
Three exclamation marks.
三个感叹号。

282
00:13:27.220 --> 00:13:30.500
Also, you should know Jenna is so adorable and very pregnant.
另外，你应该知道珍娜现在非常可爱，而且怀着孕。

283
00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:32.460
She's going to have a baby boy.
她要生个小男孩了。

284
00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:35.020
And Isabel is as sassy as they come.
伊莎贝尔也一如既往地俏皮可爱。

285
00:13:35.360 --> 00:13:37.760
I hope you all are well and the kiddos are great.
希望你们一切都好，孩子们也都很好。

286
00:13:38.180 --> 00:13:41.340
Also, I'm still having problems with my damn sprinklers.
另外，我那该死的喷水装置还是有问题。

287
00:13:41.520 --> 00:13:44.420
And of course, I think of you and Nancy laughing whenever they break.
当然，每次它们坏掉的时候，我都会想起你和南希的笑声。

288
00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:50.040
Because I would talk to him all the time about my homeowner like issues.
因为我总是会跟他聊这些房主才会遇到的琐事。

289
00:13:50.540 --> 00:13:52.760
But lady, we were so excited.
天哪，我们当时真的太兴奋了。

290
00:13:53.080 --> 00:13:57.900
I love that you were so excited about it that you put it in your little email update to Steve,
我喜欢你当时那么兴奋，甚至还特意在给史蒂夫的邮件更新里提到了这件事，

291
00:13:58.060 --> 00:14:00.020
which you would do, which was the sweetest thing.
你确实会这么做，这真是最贴心的举动。

292
00:14:00.100 --> 00:14:03.740
And I know he loved because he would get a little glimpse into how things were going.
我知道他肯定很喜欢，因为他能从中一窥我们的近况。

293
00:14:04.040 --> 00:14:04.260
Yes.
是的。

294
00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:06.740
And he always would respond back to what they were up to.
而且他总是会回复我们当时在忙些什么。

295
00:14:07.140 --> 00:14:08.360
You know how we feel about Steve.
你知道我们对史蒂夫的感觉。

296
00:14:08.520 --> 00:14:09.260
He's just the beSt.
他简直是最棒的。

