1117
00:50:35.720 --> 00:50:38.300
In the first scene of Hamlet, Horatio says,
在《哈姆雷特》的第一场戏中，霍拉旭说道：

1118
00:50:38.540 --> 00:50:43.800
Now, sir, young Fortenbra, of unimproved metal, hot and full, hath in the skirts of Norway
“先生，年轻的福丁布拉，血气方刚，未经磨练，在挪威边境

1119
00:50:43.800 --> 00:50:47.560
here and there, sharked up a list of landless resolutes.
四处搜罗了一群无地的亡命之徒。”

1120
00:50:48.880 --> 00:50:51.000
This led me to myshakespeare.com.
这引导我找到了 myshakespeare.com 网站。

1121
00:50:51.460 --> 00:50:52.680
What a delight!
真是太棒了！

1122
00:50:53.400 --> 00:50:56.060
It was wonderful and fascinating.
既精彩又迷人。

1123
00:50:56.520 --> 00:51:02.040
First of all, they explained the list of landless resolutes, which many modern English speakers
首先，他们解释了“无地的亡命之徒”中的“list”，许多现代英语使用者

1124
00:51:02.040 --> 00:51:06.160
would think that the word list refers to the list of names of men who have signed on for
可能会认为这里的“list”是指那些报名参加

1125
00:51:06.160 --> 00:51:07.080
the military campaign.
军事行动的人员名单。

1126
00:51:07.440 --> 00:51:09.900
But that was not the case with Shakespeare's audience.
但莎士比亚当时的观众并不是这样理解的。

1127
